%N A358321 a(n) is the index of the smallest n-gonal number with exactly n distinct prime factors.
%H A358321 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24103849">Extending A358321 by prime-power enumeration and arithmetic exclusions</a>, 2026.
%H A358321 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A358321/a358321.txt">Table of indices, polygonal values and prime factorizations for n = 3..19</a>
%H A358321 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/DistinctPrimeFactors.html">Distinct Prime Factors</a>
%H A358321 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PolygonalNumber.html">Polygonal Number</a>
%F A358321 a(n) = (sqrt((n-4)^2 + 8*(n-2)*A358862(n)) + n-4)/(2*(n-2)). - _Carlo Corti_, Nov 10 2026
%e A358321 a(3) = 11 because the 11th triangular number is 66 = 2*3*11, and no earlier triangular number has 3 distinct prime factors. - _Carlo Corti_, Nov 10 2026
